WEBVTT

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:11.220
The history of gaming extends 5,000 
years into the past to ancient Egypt.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:15.720
Ancient games foretold the 
futures of men and kings.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:19.200
They were magic ceremonies that 
determined a person's fate.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.340
These ceremonies were known 
as the "Shadow Games."

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.990
In the present, a young boy 
solves the Millennium Puzzle.

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:30.210
He becomes the heir to the Shadow Games.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:38.300
This boy possesses two hearts - 
one of light and one of darkness.

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:42.210
He is known as "Yu-Gi-Oh."

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:50.340
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:57.250
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:04.000
Game cartridges are stacked 
in the corner of the room

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:10.700
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:15.800
You're on the other side of the table

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:19.170
I'm talking to you, but...

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:26.100
You don't change your 
facial expression at all

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:32.350
Even though I'm this close to you

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:39.620
These feelings don't reach 
you, don't reach you

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:46.360
What is truly precious?

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:56.010
Stolen Blue-Eyes White Dragon

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:47.690
It's time to eat.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:51.020
What?

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:53.520
Oh no!

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:15.450
It's always hilarious!

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:18.570
Excuse me.

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:21.010
Master Pegasus.

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:29.690
The world's finest wine, gorgonzola 
cheese and comic book.

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:33.120
This is when I'm happiest.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:35.600
You do realize that, don't you?

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:37.560
I'm sorry to interrupt.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:41.360
Never mind.  What is it?

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:44.690
A certain boy escaped from the castle.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:48.880
Even though I invited him as a guest?

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:53.370
Perhaps he didn't enjoy our hospitality.

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:55.930
Well, there's no need to worry.

00:03:56.440 --> 00:04:00.530
I know what he has planned.

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:03.850
Six hours have passed since dueling began.

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:07.730
12 of the 40 participants 
have been eliminated.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:12.600
The losers are leaving by boat.

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:15.060
What about him?

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:18.470
Yugi Muto has five Star Chips.

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:21.960
Wonderful.  Impressive, Yugi boy.

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:27.060
I need him to keep winning 
and come to this castle.

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:30.440
I must keep my eye on Yugi boy.

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:33.960
That other boy will eventually go to him.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:38.720
When you catch him, lock him in the 
dungeon so that he can't escape again.

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:39.360
Yes sir.

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:44.850
That was an unexpected distraction.

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:48.490
I'll wait quietly until the proper time.

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:59.640
Ryota Kajiki is a hard guy to hate.

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:03.850
All duelists came here with 
their own hopes and dreams.

00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:08.280
Yeah.  They have their own 
problems, just like us.

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:10.170
Problems...

00:05:14.440 --> 00:05:16.090
You're right.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:18.770
What's that?

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:21.000
Help me!

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:23.600
Let go of me!  Someone save me!

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:25.500
Hold it right there!

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:27.480
Help me!

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:29.010
All right!

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:33.770
Nailed it.

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:43.840
Let go of me!

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:45.460
Quit resisting, kid.

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:46.540
Stop it!

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:48.730
You won't get away with this!

00:05:48.730 --> 00:05:50.200
There's no need for violence.

00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:54.800
It's for your own good 
that you don't interfere.

00:05:55.030 --> 00:05:58.120
This guy lost all his Star Chips.

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:02.080
You're wrong!  My Star Chips 
and cards were stolen from me!

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:03.320
It doesn't matter.

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:07.560
If you lose all your Star Chips, 
you're deported from this island.

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:11.410
Those are the rules.  Give up.

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:14.290
Ouch...  Damn...

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:20.060
Here's another one.

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:24.160
How annoying!

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:27.000
I won the national tournament, you know!

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.090
Make more room.

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:34.100
If only my Star Chips didn't get stolen...

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:35.670
Hey!

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:37.490
You!

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:41.410
What did the person who stole 
your Star Chips look like?

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:45.600
I didn't see his face because 
he covered it with a bandanna.

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:48.220
He suddenly challenged me to a duel.

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:50.720
Was it at the Duel Ring in the grasslands?

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:54.820
Yeah.  When I placed my Star 
Chips and my deck on the table,

00:06:54.820 --> 00:06:56.330
he stole them and ran off!

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:59.860
We'll find that thief, so just wait!

00:07:00.430 --> 00:07:02.840
This boat departs in 30 minutes.

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:04.880
That's your time limit.

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:07.280
We'll find the thief!

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:09.120
We'll find him and teach him a lesson!

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:12.560
Yeah!  For a duelist, Star Chips 
are the same as his own life.

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:17.280
I won't forgive anyone who 
steals those Star Chips!

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:18.740
Thank you.

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:20.150
By the way...

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:25.020
When I catch the thief, I'll take 
half of your Star Chips as a reward.

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:25.760
C'mon now.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:29.570
All right, let's go!

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:32.170
What nonsense was that?

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:34.350
I was joking.

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:40.600
But how are we supposed to find 
this thief without a single clue?

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:44.570
His Star Chips were stolen at that Duel Ring.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:50.800
What are you doing, Yugi?

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:53.950
They say that a criminal always 
returns to the scene of the crime.

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:55.600
That's true.

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:57.720
Let's take a nap.

00:07:57.720 --> 00:08:01.650
Will we really find the thief this way?

00:08:03.640 --> 00:08:06.020
I found you, Yugi!

00:08:06.020 --> 00:08:08.280
He must be the one we're looking for!

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:09.160
I'll beat him up!

00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:11.200
No!  Don't use violence!

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:12.470
Yugi.

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:13.520
You punk!

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:16.760
Give back the Star Chips you stole.

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:17.640
Wait.

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:20.650
I think he's here for me.

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:23.800
Do you want to duel me?

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:24.810
Yeah.

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:38.920
If he tries to steal Yugi's 
Star Chips, I'll make him pay!

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:41.410
Yeah!  We won't let him escape!

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:53.780
How many Star Chips will you wager?

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:58.920
Fine.  I'll wager all of my Star Chips.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:05.460
Is he actually...

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:08.860
He isn't wearing a Dueling Glove.

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:13.070
That means he definitely is the thief.

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:18.220
Why would Yugi accept a duel from a 
thief when we're running out of time?

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:22.960
Maybe Yugi knows his true identity.

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:24.130
Duel!

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:29.250
Here I go.  I will avenge my brother.

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:44.090
It's no good.

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:47.230
What's wrong, big brother?

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:50.200
Damn.  In my current state, 
I can't defeat Yugi.

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:51.560
That's not true!

00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:55.240
You always said that cards 
are all about power.

00:09:55.440 --> 00:10:00.000
But the power of my cards lost 
against the heart of Yugi's cards.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.880
I can't defeat him until I 
understand the heart of the cards.

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:05.130
Big brother...

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:09.850
Mokuba, hold on to this for me.

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:13.970
It holds the data to open the

00:10:13.970 --> 00:10:17.390
storage facility that houses Kaiba 
Corporation's important documents.

00:10:18.440 --> 00:10:19.970
But why?

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:21.700
I'm going on a journey for a while.

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:23.960
Mokuba, you're in charge while I'm gone.

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:25.770
Wait, big brother!

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:31.540
Yugi, I will defeat you.

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:39.380
I  play Man-Eating Plant in attack position.

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:41.430
It's my turn.

00:10:41.430 --> 00:10:45.650
I'll fight back with this card!

00:10:46.600 --> 00:10:48.810
Winged Dragon, Guardian of the Fortress #1.

00:11:21.730 --> 00:11:23.800
Fireball Stone!

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:37.600
You can't defeat my monster 
using stolen cards.

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:41.680
Because your heart doesn't 
dwell inside stolen cards.

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:46.120
Yugi, I don't believe in 
your "heart of the cards!"

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:49.720
Cards aren't about heart!  
Cards are about power!

00:11:49.880 --> 00:11:56.170
Like I thought, you're Mokuba, 
Seto Kaiba's younger brother.

00:11:57.800 --> 00:11:59.160
Shut up!

00:11:59.160 --> 00:11:59.920
That kid...

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:01.230
Kaiba‘s little brother?

00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:06.360
My brother vanished because 
you hurt his pride.

00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:11.180
It's your fault that Pegasus is now 
trying to take over Kaiba Corporation!

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:13.110
What?  Pegasus?

00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:20.050
Pegasus spread the news that you 
defeated my brother worldwide.

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:25.950
Since then, Kaiba Corporation has 
lost the trust of its investors,

00:12:25.950 --> 00:12:28.620
and business has plummeted.

00:12:29.360 --> 00:12:32.450
That's what Pegasus was waiting for.

00:12:33.240 --> 00:12:38.960
Transfer all your shares 
in Kaiba Corporation to me.

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:44.530
That's the only way we can 
rebuild Kaiba Corporation.

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:49.800
We understand, but we have one condition.

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:50.880
Yes?

00:12:50.880 --> 00:12:56.320
Yugi is responsible for destroying 
this company's reputation.

00:12:56.320 --> 00:13:01.490
To restore trust in this 
company, you must defeat him.

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:06.980
Mr. Pegasus, if you succeed, the board will

00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:10.700
no longer have Seto Kaiba 
as the company's president.

00:13:10.960 --> 00:13:16.210
We promise to give Kaiba Corporation to you.

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:21.360
Defeating Yugi will be very easy.

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:23.150
One more thing.

00:13:23.720 --> 00:13:27.630
Seto Kaiba's brother Mokuba has the 
key to the storage facility that

00:13:27.630 --> 00:13:30.360
houses the company's important documents.

00:13:30.360 --> 00:13:35.030
Oh, no problem.  Leave that to me as well.

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:45.080
Hey!  Let me go!

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:47.840
I'll never tell you where I hid the key!

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:53.320
Mokuba boy, I invite you 
as a guest to my Kingdom.

00:13:53.320 --> 00:13:58.180
You'll want to hand over the key after 
you experience our wonderful hospitality.

00:13:58.180 --> 00:14:00.410
Let me go!

00:14:01.720 --> 00:14:04.520
Yugi, it's all your fault!

00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:06.050
I understand the situation,

00:14:06.050 --> 00:14:10.130
but that's no excuse for 
stealing other people's cards.

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:13.250
Be quiet!  I play this next!

00:14:15.070 --> 00:14:17.330
Go, Krokodilus!

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:30.040
It's pointless to keep dueling.

00:14:30.040 --> 00:14:34.440
This game isn't so simple that 
you can win with stolen cards.

00:14:34.440 --> 00:14:38.560
That's right!  Stealing Star 
Chips for revenge is the worst!

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:40.560
You're wrong!  You have the wrong idea!

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:45.050
I have to protect Kaiba Corporation 
in my brother's place!

00:14:45.560 --> 00:14:48.930
If he steals Yugi's Star 
Chips and disqualifies him,

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:53.540
that means Yugi technically 
never lost a duel.

00:14:53.960 --> 00:14:55.480
What do you mean?

00:14:55.480 --> 00:14:56.960
You don't understand?

00:14:56.960 --> 00:14:58.240
Do you?

00:14:58.240 --> 00:15:00.850
Well, no.  What do you mean?

00:15:01.680 --> 00:15:06.560
If Yugi doesn't lose in a duel, Pegasus's 
agreement with The Big Five is void.

00:15:06.560 --> 00:15:07.820
I see.

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:10.590
Mokuba!

00:15:11.960 --> 00:15:13.690
In that case...

00:15:13.690 --> 00:15:15.030
Stop, Mokuba!

00:15:17.530 --> 00:15:18.700
Stop, you punk!

00:15:18.700 --> 00:15:24.130
Mokuba, you can't save 
Kaiba Corporation that way.

00:15:24.700 --> 00:15:26.910
Kaiba is suffering right now.

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:30.000
But that's so he can learn 
about the heart of the cards.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:34.180
He's fighting to win his pride back.

00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:38.400
Kaiba will return when he learns 
about the heart of the cards.

00:15:38.400 --> 00:15:44.140
Are you willing to abandon your brother 
and the trust in Kaiba Corporation?

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:45.810
But...

00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:49.860
But what should I do?

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:52.200
You don't need to steal.

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:56.010
I promise to defeat Pegasus.

00:15:56.560 --> 00:16:00.340
If you want to know what 
Kaiba is struggling with...

00:16:00.550 --> 00:16:03.780
If you want to understand 
the heart of the cards,

00:16:03.780 --> 00:16:08.350
give that boy back his 
deck and his Star Chips.

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:12.320
I understand.  I trust you, Yugi.

00:16:12.560 --> 00:16:14.840
The boat is leaving in three minutes!

00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:16.370
Let's hurry, Mokuba!

00:16:24.640 --> 00:16:27.770
C'mon!  You're also rowing for me!

00:16:27.770 --> 00:16:30.410
No!  The boat!

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:36.520
The losers' boat already left.

00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:40.410
But they shouldn't have 
left for another minute!

00:16:41.240 --> 00:16:42.950
I don't care.

00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:45.720
You tricked us!

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:50.410
I'll return these Star Chips, 
so call the boat back!

00:16:51.590 --> 00:16:52.830
What?

00:16:57.000 --> 00:17:01.220
Hey!  Those included some 
of Yugi's Star Chips!

00:17:01.220 --> 00:17:03.080
I'm sorry, Yugi.

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:08.080
If you have your Star Chips stolen, 
then you're a disgrace as a duelist.

00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:10.740
That alone is enough to disqualify you.

00:17:13.120 --> 00:17:14.160
Mokuba!

00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:19.410
The only way to gain Star 
Chips is to win duels.

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:25.040
Let's hurry back before 
Pegasus gets worried, Mokuba.

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:25.990
Let me go.

00:17:26.240 --> 00:17:27.290
Wait.

00:17:28.160 --> 00:17:31.400
I still have three Star Chips left.

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:35.230
I'll wager them all in a duel against you!

00:17:36.480 --> 00:17:39.280
I don't duel.

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:44.640
But if you want to duel that badly, 
I'll find an opponent for you.

00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:47.930
Come back to that Duel Ring in an hour.

00:18:04.360 --> 00:18:07.730
How could Yugi fight that well?

00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:14.520
I wasn't weaker than Yugi.

00:18:14.520 --> 00:18:16.640
My only conclusion is...

00:18:18.800 --> 00:18:22.650
He was fighting for 
something more than I was.

00:18:25.480 --> 00:18:28.130
Impossible!  Exodia?

00:18:37.520 --> 00:18:40.160
His grandfather gave him those cards.

00:18:40.160 --> 00:18:43.470
He was battling to protect 
the heart of the cards.

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:52.240
This new system has all the 
functions of a supercomputer.

00:18:52.240 --> 00:18:54.870
I can duel anytime, anyplace.

00:18:54.870 --> 00:18:59.990
When I finish building it, I can 
battle Yugi on equal footing.

00:19:07.800 --> 00:19:09.230
Don't move!

00:19:09.230 --> 00:19:13.090
Seto Kaiba, you're coming with us.

00:19:13.440 --> 00:19:17.700
Fine.  I know you won't 
accept "no" as an answer.

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:21.690
Thanks for being reasonable.

00:19:23.940 --> 00:19:25.110
Damn!

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:30.280
What?

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:36.880
Suicide.

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:39.290
It saves us the trouble of locking him up.

00:19:52.140 --> 00:19:54.730
Let me go!

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:55.740
Yugi!

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:58.600
Mokuba!  Let him go!

00:19:58.600 --> 00:20:00.840
I'll consider it if you win the duel.

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:02.210
Who's my opponent?

00:20:02.210 --> 00:20:04.920
He's already here.  Look!

00:20:11.920 --> 00:20:13.450
Kaiba?

00:20:14.280 --> 00:20:15.690
Big brother!

00:20:19.040 --> 00:20:22.280
Yugi, I'll get my revenge!

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:26.250
I'll get my revenge!

00:20:32.310 --> 00:20:34.600
Why is Kaiba here?

00:20:34.600 --> 00:20:37.360
What?  That's Kaiba's ghost?

00:20:37.360 --> 00:20:39.920
He died hating Yugi?

00:20:39.920 --> 00:20:43.800
Yugi, don't believe him!  
It must be Pegasus's trap!

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:49.800
But he's attacking Yugi with Blue-Eyes 
White Dragon, a card that only Kaiba has.

00:20:49.800 --> 00:20:53.400
Don't lose, Yugi!  Uncover his true identity!

00:20:53.400 --> 00:20:57.040
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Resurrection!  Magical Hats

00:20:57.040 --> 00:20:58.970
Duel, standby!

00:21:01.860 --> 00:21:10.260
The flask glistens

00:21:11.300 --> 00:21:18.110
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:18.600 --> 00:21:27.080
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:27.780 --> 00:21:34.850
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:40.690
Shower of happiness

00:21:40.980 --> 00:21:44.800
I will shower you with it

00:21:45.130 --> 00:21:53.080
I will support you even when you feel lonely

00:21:53.280 --> 00:21:57.310
Shower of happiness

